(7413095, 1168354, 13891, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your votes and comments.<br/>This is the church that appears in the funeral scenes of the film "Four Weddings and a Funeral". It is located in Essex in southern England and has been restored to its former glory by its neighbours Proctor &amp; Gamble, who manufacture soap products in the factory next door. The church Is no longer used, but is open to the public on selected weekends during the year. The graveyard is maintained as a nature reserve, and remains as consecrated ground.</td>', 'Thank you all for your votes and comments.This is the church that appears in the funeral scenes of the film "Four Weddings and a Funeral". It is located in Essex in southern England and has been restored to its former glory by its neighbours Proctor & Gamble, who manufacture soap products in the factory next door. The church Is no longer used, but is open to the public on selected weekends during the year. The graveyard is maintained as a nature reserve, and remains as consecrated ground.', '2015-10-30 03:04:35.000000', NULL, 0),
